---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Contour from '../components/Contour.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Next Steppe" description="A xeriscape design and planning practice built on stormwater and hydrology expertise, based in the Vail Valley.">
  <section class="wrap about">
    <span class="eyebrow">Practice Notes</span>
    <h1>Designed from the water down.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Most landscape plans start with plants and work backward. This one starts with where
      the water goes &mdash; snowmelt, runoff, storm events &mdash; and builds the planting plan on top of that.
    </p>

    <div class="grid-2 about-grid">
      <div>
        <h2>Background</h2>
        <p>
          Trained in landscape architecture with a specialization in stormwater management,
          bioinfiltration, and rain garden design — now practiced as xeriscape design and
          planning. That background shapes every project: soil and drainage come first, plant
          selection follows, and the result is a landscape that holds up through the valley's
          dry summers and short, intense storm events.
        </p>
        <p>
          Based in the Vail Valley, working across mountain-town lots, HOA common areas, and
          properties where water-wise design has to hold up against deer, altitude, and a short
          growing season.
        </p>
        <p>
          That same discipline runs through the <a href="/plants">plant database</a> published
          here &mdash; 100 xeric species with sourced water, elevation and fire data. Where a
          figure has a published source it is cited; where it doesn&rsquo;t, the entry says so
          rather than filling the gap with an estimate.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Approach</h2>
        <ul class="approach-list">
          <li><span class="tag">01</span> Read the site &mdash; grading, drainage, sun, existing soil.</li>
          <li><span class="tag">02</span> Plan the water &mdash; infiltration, detention, and where runoff is meant to go.</li>
          <li><span class="tag">03</span> Select xeric, regionally adapted plants once the water plan is set.</li>
          <li><span class="tag">04</span> Design for maintenance that actually fits a mountain-town schedule.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <Contour />

    <div class="stamp about-stamp">
      <span class="compass">&#8593;N</span>BLA &middot; MSLA, STORMWATER MANAGEMENT SPECIALIZATION &middot; VAIL VALLEY, CO
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about { padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; }
  .lead { max-width: 640px; font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--basalt-soft); }
  .about-grid { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .approach-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.8rem; }
  .approach-list li { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.7rem; }
  .about-stamp { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
</style>
